WEBVTT

00:00:00.738 --> 00:00:01.812
Welcome to Prac360:

00:00:01.812 --> 00:00:04.921
the complete practice system for South African doctors.

00:00:04.921 --> 00:00:15.489
In the next few minutes we'll walk through a normal day in a practice, from the first booking to the payment from the medical aid, and show you how Prac360 takes the admin off your hands.

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:17.939
Here is what we will cover:

00:00:17.939 --> 00:00:30.639
the home dashboard and front desk, the patient file, consultations with AI Scribe, billing and claims, payments and stock, the optional modules, Assist, and how your team stays safe and supported.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.452
Everyone signs in with their own login.

00:00:33.452 --> 00:00:41.412
Two-step verification adds a code from your phone, so your patients' information stays protected, and each person only sees what their role allows.

00:00:42.115 --> 00:00:44.546
The Home Dashboard is your morning briefing.

00:00:44.546 --> 00:00:51.618
Turnover and collections this month, what medical aids and patients owe, today's appointments and anything that needs attention.

00:00:54.316 --> 00:01:00.327
Messages from Prac360 appear right on the dashboard, and you can collapse them when you've read them.

00:01:00.327 --> 00:01:05.862
Each person can also arrange the dashboard their own way, and choose day, dusk or night mode.

00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:09.623
The diary is built for a busy front desk.

00:01:09.623 --> 00:01:17.610
Each doctor has a column, appointments show their status, and you change the status with one click as the patient arrives, goes in and leaves.

00:01:20.517 --> 00:01:25.012
A little red marker shows who was seen but not billed yet, so nothing slips through.

00:01:25.012 --> 00:01:30.148
No-shows are marked automatically, and the oncology treatment chairs sit right beside the diary.

00:01:31.721 --> 00:01:32.905
Booking takes seconds.

00:01:32.905 --> 00:01:37.860
Choose the patient, and the doctor, time and length are filled in from the slot you clicked.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.661
Overlapping bookings are stopped before they happen.

00:01:42.721 --> 00:01:47.324
Registering a new patient is one simple form, with compulsory fields clearly marked.

00:01:47.324 --> 00:01:55.928
The medical aid membership can be checked online, and with the patient's consent their record is shared with other Prac360 practices through their ID number.

00:01:56.922 --> 00:02:00.288
The patient file shows the whole patient on one screen:

00:02:00.288 --> 00:02:06.651
medical aid, allergies, chronic medicines and conditions, visits, documents, the account and follow-ups.

00:02:08.122 --> 00:02:09.799
Some doctors like to type.

00:02:09.799 --> 00:02:12.959
The Classic consultation is a clean, simple note:

00:02:12.959 --> 00:02:18.763
history, examination, diagnosis and plan, with smart ICD-10 search and your own templates.

00:02:20.124 --> 00:02:21.538
Others prefer to talk.

00:02:21.538 --> 00:02:29.510
With AI Scribe, and only with the patient's permission, Prac360 listens to the consultation and fills in the note as you go:

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:36.646
the complaint and how long, the vital signs, the examination, the diagnosis with its ICD-10 code, and the plan.

00:02:42.526 --> 00:02:49.691
Notice that it linked the ICD-10 code by itself, and that it learns from your choices, so there is less to check every time.

00:02:49.691 --> 00:02:52.002
It also works when the patient is quiet:

00:02:52.002 --> 00:02:53.736
just say the details yourself.

00:02:55.727 --> 00:02:57.364
When you finish, you review.

00:02:57.364 --> 00:03:02.510
Anything that needs a second look is listed, and the fix button corrects it in one step.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.375
Nothing is signed or billed until you approve it.

00:03:09.926 --> 00:03:18.344
The clinical dashboard and follow-up manager keep track of chronic patients, results to review and recalls, so patients don't fall through the cracks.

00:03:20.127 --> 00:03:23.951
Signing the note creates the bill with the right tariff codes.

00:03:23.951 --> 00:03:33.694
Before anything is sent, Prac360 checks the codes, modifiers and ICD-10 rules, and the optional SAMA billing coach checks every line against the coding rules.

00:03:34.394 --> 00:03:38.172
Claims go to the medical aids electronically, through the switch.

00:03:38.172 --> 00:03:41.775
On the awaiting payment list you see every claim's EDI status:

00:03:41.775 --> 00:03:48.634
sent, passed the switch check, accepted by the medical aid, and waiting for payment, with a warning when it's overdue.

00:03:49.335 --> 00:03:55.303
If a claim is rejected, Prac360 explains why in plain language, and who rejected it.

00:03:55.303 --> 00:03:56.511
Step one, fix it:

00:03:56.511 --> 00:04:00.631
for example the dependant code or an authorisation number.

00:04:00.631 --> 00:04:03.686
Step two, re-send it by EDI with one click.

00:04:05.537 --> 00:04:10.418
When the medical aid pays, the electronic remittance is imported and reconciled automatically.

00:04:10.418 --> 00:04:14.053
Short payments move to the patient's account, ready for the statement.

00:04:15.738 --> 00:04:19.158
Payments and accounts keep the money side simple:

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:26.279
capture cash, card or EFT in seconds, print or email statements, and see the age analysis at a glance.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:34.097
Reports cover everything from turnover and collections to rejections, debtors and stock, on screen, as PDF or Excel.

00:04:36.181 --> 00:04:44.575
With stock and dispensing, medicines are tracked by batch and expiry, you are warned when it's time to order, and dispensed items are billed straight from stock.

00:04:46.387 --> 00:04:54.363
For practices that admit patients, the hospital and wards module gives you a ward board, admissions, authorisations, theatre and the hospital account.

00:04:56.587 --> 00:05:00.902
The oncology module follows the cancer patient from referral to follow-up:

00:05:00.902 --> 00:05:09.358
treatment plans and cycles, nursing and pharmacy checks, authorisations, and treatment chairs, where you put a patient in a chair with one click.

00:05:10.789 --> 00:05:13.156
Every practice gets the core system.

00:05:13.156 --> 00:05:15.261
Then you add only what you need:

00:05:15.261 --> 00:05:24.733
Assist and AI Scribe, stock and dispensing, hospital and wards, oncology, dental, the SAMA billing coach, advanced reports and priority support.

00:05:25.435 --> 00:05:28.709
Assist is like a personal assistant inside Prac360.

00:05:28.709 --> 00:05:30.892
Ask it anything in your own words:

00:05:30.892 --> 00:05:37.121
what do I need to do today, what allergies does Thandiwe have, or take me to the rejected claims.

00:05:39.436 --> 00:05:41.283
It also does the work for you.

00:05:41.283 --> 00:05:49.535
Tell it that a patient is allergic to aspirin, that Ayesha paid three hundred and fifty rand cash, or to book Pieter on Friday at ten.

00:05:49.535 --> 00:05:51.998
If something is missing, it simply asks.

00:05:53.437 --> 00:05:56.298
Your team stays connected with internal messages.

00:05:56.298 --> 00:06:02.836
Send a message to everyone or to one person; it pops up to be acknowledged, but never interrupts a consultation.

00:06:03.537 --> 00:06:05.481
Found a problem or have an idea?

00:06:05.481 --> 00:06:07.425
Report it straight from Prac360.

00:06:07.425 --> 00:06:12.407
The Prac360 team sees it, can ask you questions, and lets you know when it's done.

00:06:13.109 --> 00:06:14.322
Training is built in.

00:06:14.322 --> 00:06:20.848
The Training Academy has short courses for every role, show me tours on the real screens, and a printable manual.

00:06:20.848 --> 00:06:24.313
What's new keeps everyone up to date with every improvement.

00:06:25.109 --> 00:06:34.316
The practice manager controls who can do what, with roles for reception, nurses, doctors, billing and management, and every change is recorded in the audit trail.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:45.510
Your data is protected with personal logins, two-step verification, roles and a full audit trail, and Prac360 is made for South Africa:

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:49.892
medical aids, ICD-10, NAPPI codes, PMBs, VAT and the rand.

00:06:50.594 --> 00:06:51.097
Prac360.

00:06:51.097 --> 00:06:53.613
Less admin, more time for your patients.

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:57.701
We'll set it up with your codes, your medical aids and your team.

00:06:57.701 --> 00:06:59.587
Book your personal demo today.

